body:
Hi there,

it's me again. As in #181 I'd like to suggest some new filters for Emails.php. 

Is there a reason why you are not using WC()->mailer->emails to loop through all registered emails instead of adding your own array with default emails only?
You could then dynamically construct the filters for subject + heading for each email instead of manually adding the filters for predefined emails only:

```php
foreach( WC()->mailer->emails as $class => $instance ) {
     $this->register_string( $instance->id );
     // Subject filter
     add_filter( 'woocommerce_email_subject_' . $instance->id, array( $this, 'translate_subject' ), 10, 2 ); 
} 
....

public function translate_subject( $subject, $order ) {
     if ( ! is_a( $order, 'WC_Order' ) )
         return $subject; 
     $email = str_replace( 'woocommerce_email_subject_', '',  current_filter() );
     return $this->translateEmailStringToOrderLanguage( $subject, $order, 'subject', $email );
}
```

this is just a draft which I didn't test yet but I think this would make things easier and extension-ready. Otherwise it would be good if methods from your Emails object could somehow be accessible for DRY reasons.

Unfortunately Polylang or Woo Poly Integration cannot present the translated up-sells or cross-sells as it requires modifying two template files (cart/cross-sells.php and single-product/up-sells.php).

I have submitted two PR to WooCommerce to add apply_filters() calls to both of these template files and submitted an issue to reference the two PR.
Issue:
https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/issues/15188
PRs:
https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/15174
https://github.com/woocommerce/woocommerce/pull/15175

This is not a bug in Polylang or Woo Poly Integration but, if it gets fixed, it will need changes to this plugin to make use of the change. Also, if you are friends with the WooCommerce developers you could encourage them to accept the PRs or make similar changes.

Here is the code I used when I made the changes on my test installation:

    add_filter( 'woocommerce_cart_up_sells_post_id', 'dsh_polylang_translate_product_id' );
    add_filter( 'woocommerce_cart_cross_sells_post_id', 'dsh_polylang_translate_product_id' );

    function dsh_polylang_translate_product_id( $related_product_id ) {
      if ( function_exists( 'pll_get_post' ) ) {
        return pll_get_post( $related_product_id );
      }
      return $related_product_id;
    }
